# NOTE ON THE LEADING SLASHES — they are load-bearing.
#
# In gitignore syntax, `ios/` matches a directory named `ios` AT ANY DEPTH.
# This project has FOUR of them:
#
#     ios/                                  <- generated, should be ignored
#     modules/levl-dual-camera/ios/         <- Swift source, must be committed
#     modules/levl-live-activity/ios/       <- Swift source, must be committed
#     modules/levl-health/ios/              <- Swift source, must be committed
#
# An unanchored `ios/` silently excludes all three native modules. That produced
# an EAS build that uploaded cleanly and then failed in prebuild, because the
# widget config plugin could not find LevlWorkoutAttributes.swift to copy.
#
# `/ios/` anchors the pattern to the repository root, which is what we want.
# Do not remove the leading slashes.

# Generated native projects. Rebuilt by `expo prebuild` from app.json plus the
# config plugins, on every machine and every EAS build — so a committed copy
# would go stale against plugins/withLevlWidgets.js.
/ios/
/android/

# CocoaPods output
/Pods/
*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/

# Expo / Metro
/.expo/
/.expo-shared/
/dist/
/web-build/
*.jsbundle

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local env
.env
.env.local
